   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 381 of the laws of 2010 amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Rye Brook, in relation\nto extending the expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7683",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7683-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 381 of 2010",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7683\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 381 of the laws of 2010 amending the tax law\nrelating to the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Rye\nBrook, in relation to extending the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize the Village of Rye Brook to extend a room occupancy tax not\nto exceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill extends the current Village of Rye Brook occupancy tax for\nanother three years until September 1, 2025.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the current Village of Rye Brook occupancy tax. The\nVillage of Rye Brook has used these non-property tax revenues to offset\ncapital expenditures.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: A65554/S5083 (Otis/MAYER) 8/29/19 SIGNED CHAP. 211\n2016: A9072/S6079 (Otis/LATIMER) 3/31/16 signed chap. 290\n2013: A3823/S2594 (Otis/LATIMER) 07/12/13 SIGNED CHAP. 108\n2010: A231-AJS1180-A (Latimer/OPPENHEIMER) 08/13/10 SIGNED CHAP .381\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThe Village estimates revenues of $720,000 per year minus implementation\ncosts.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
